# My Projects

A collection of my web development projects, showcasing my learning, practical implementation, and hands-on experience with different web technologies.

## Projects

### 1. Newsletter Sign-Up Page

#### Project Overview

A responsive newsletter sign-up page built with HTML5 and CSS3. This project focuses on creating a clean, responsive form layout with interactive styling and native HTML5 validation.

#### Live Demo

 https://ishratalib.github.io/NewsLetterCard/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/NewsLetterCard.git

### 2. O-Tech — IT Solutions & Services Website

#### Project Overview

A responsive IT solutions and services website built with HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, JavaScript, jQuery, and Owl Carousel. The project features a modern business-style interface with services, case studies, testimonials, pricing, team information, and contact sections.

#### Live Demo

https://ishratotech.netlify.app/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/Otech.git

### 3. JavaScript Practice

#### Project Overview

A simple JavaScript practice project created to strengthen understanding of fundamental JavaScript concepts through small console-based exercises involving loops, functions, arrow functions, and arrays.

#### Live Demo

No live demo available. This project is designed to run JavaScript exercises through the browser console.

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/JavaScript-Practice.git

### 4. JavaScript Brain Teasers

#### Project Overview

A JavaScript practice project containing brain teasers and output-prediction questions focused on understanding values, references, objects, copying, mutation, and memory behavior in JavaScript.

#### Live Demo

No live demo available. This is a console-based JavaScript practice project.

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/JavaScript-Brain-Teasers.git

### 5. JavaScript To Do App

#### Project Overview

A simple and interactive To Do application built with HTML5, JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS. The project allows users to add, complete, edit, and delete tasks while practicing DOM manipulation, event handling, arrays, objects, and application logic.

#### Live Demo

 https://ishratalib.github.io/JavaScript-ToDo-App/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/JavaScript-ToDo-App.git

### 6. Admin Dashboard

#### Project Overview

A responsive admin dashboard built with HTML5, JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS. The project includes frontend authentication using Local Storage, protected dashboard access, logout functionality, and a dynamic users directory powered by the DummyJSON API.

#### Live Demo

https://ishratalib.github.io/Admin-Dashboard/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/Admin-Dashboard.git

### 7. Weather Dashboard

#### Project Overview

A responsive weather dashboard built with HTML5, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS, Chart.js, and WeatherAPI. The application allows users to search for cities, view current weather conditions, check a 5-day forecast, explore air-quality information, view sunrise and sunset times, and save favourite cities.

#### Live Demo

https://ishratalib.github.io/weatherdashboard/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/weatherdashboard.git

### 8. React To-Do App

#### Project Overview

A simple and responsive To-Do application built with React and Vite. This project focuses on practicing React fundamentals, state management, event handling, dynamic UI rendering, and component-based development through a practical task-management application.

#### Live Demo

https://ishratalib.github.io/ReactToDo/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/ReactToDo.git

### 9. React Routes

#### Project Overview

A React application built to practice and demonstrate client-side routing using React Router. The project includes multiple pages, nested routes, dynamic product routes, protected routes, and a custom 404 page.

#### Live Demo

https://react-routes-project.netlify.app/

#### GitHub Repository

https://github.com/Ishratalib/React-Routes.git


